  "problem": "Let\n$E=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 5 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]$\nand\n$F=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$ Then, the dimensions of $EF$ are{{field-1}}$\\times $\n{{field-2}}.",
  "worked_solution": "We notice that $E$ is a $3\\times 2$ matrix and $F$ is a $2\\times 1$ matrix. \n\nThere are $2$ columns in $E$ and $2$ rows in $F.$ Since the number of columns in $E$ equals the number of rows in $F,$ the matrices $E$ and $F$ are conformable for multiplication. \n\nThe product $EF$ has dimensions $3\\times 1:$ \n\n$$\n{E}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{2}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{F}_{\\boxed{\\text{2}}\\times 1}={EF}_{3\\times 1}\n$$",
